      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking even a small dose of Advil alongside aspirin can still raise the risk of bleeding because both drugs influence blood clotting. Variations in individual bodies' responses don't negate the inherent risks, especially with daily aspirin use. The discomfort may seem to outweigh perceived minor risks, but not knowing your specific circumstances is concerning. An urgent appointment might be necessary, and over-the-counter pain relievers are typically used with more frequent guidance. Addressing the underlying cause of back pain is also crucial.",
